The results of the observations are expressed graphically in @fig_77. The upper is the curve for the observations at noon, and the lower that for the evening observations. The dotted curves represent _one eighth_ of the theoretical displacements. It seems fair to conclude from the figure that if there is any displacement due to the relative motion of the earth and the luminiferous aether, this cannot be much greater than 0.01 of the distance between the fringes.

